ok [*] carries :db/id
ok [*] lists card-many values in index order
ok a ref to an ident renders with the ident
ok a component is pulled in full under [*]
ok a plain ref renders as {:db/id e}
ok an entity with no datoms pulls as nil
ok a lookup ref resolves the entity
ok an ident resolves the entity
{:db/id 4294967296, :person/name Ann, :person/age 30}
ok a missing attribute is omitted
{:db/id 4294967302, :person/name Di, :person/boss {:db/id 4294967301, :person/name Cy}}
{:db/id 4294967302, :person/name Di, :person/boss {:db/id 4294967301, :person/name Cy, :person/boss {:db/id 4294967296, :person/name Ann}}}
{:db/id 4294967301, :person/name Cy, :person/friend [{:db/id 4294967296, :person/name Ann} {:db/id 4294967300, :person/name Bob}]}
ok a nested spec wins over *
{:db/id 4294967296, :person/name Ann, :person/_boss [{:db/id 4294967300} {:db/id 4294967301}]}
{:db/id 4294967296, :person/name Ann, :person/_boss [{:db/id 4294967300, :person/name Bob} {:db/id 4294967301, :person/name Cy}]}
ok a reverse component attribute pulls its one owner in full
ok a reverse attribute with no referrers is omitted
{:db/id 4294967302, :person/name Di, :person/boss {:db/id 4294967301, :person/name Cy, :person/boss {:db/id 4294967296, :person/name Ann}}}
{:db/id 4294967302, :person/name Di, :person/boss {:db/id 4294967301, :person/name Cy, :person/boss {:db/id 4294967296}}}
{:db/id 4294967303, :person/name Ed, :person/friend [{:db/id 4294967303}]}
{:db/id 4294967304, :node/label n1, :edge/to [{:db/id 4294967305, :node/label n2, :edge/to [{:db/id 4294967306, :node/label n3, :edge/to [{:db/id 4294967304}]}]}]}
{:db/id 4294967304, :node/label n1, :edge/to [{:db/id 4294967305, :node/label n2, :edge/to [{:db/id 4294967306}]}]}
ok depth 0 is the plain ref
ok :limit cuts card-many values
ok (limit attr n) is the same spec
ok :limit nil lifts the cut
ok :limit 0 omits the attribute
ok :default fills a missing attribute
ok :default does not replace a present one
ok (default attr v) is the same spec
ok :as renames the key
ok :as takes any value as the key
{:db/id 4294967301, :pal [{:db/id 4294967296, :person/name Ann}]}
ok the current view sees the update
ok as-of before the update sees the old facts
ok an older db-value is unchanged
ok since shows only the new facts
ok since has nothing for an untouched entity
[{:db/id 4294967296, :person/name Ann} {:db/id 4294967300, :person/name Bob} nil {:db/id 37}]
ok pull-many over a list
ok pull-many over nothing
{:error :nextomic/history-view, :message entity and pull read a current, as-of or since db-value, not a history one}
{:error :nextomic/pull-syntax, :message 42 in a pull pattern is no attribute, *, map or attribute expression, :clause 1}
{:error :nextomic/pull-syntax, :message :limit takes a non-negative integer or nil, not :lots, :clause 0}
{:error :kind-mismatch, :message kind mismatch}
{:error :nextomic/tx-data, :message a lookup ref needs a unique attribute, :attr :person/name}
{:error :nextomic/no-entity, :message [:person/email "nobody@x"] names no entity, :value [:person/email nobody@x]}
{:error :nextomic/unknown-attribute, :message :person/nope names no attribute, :attr :person/nope}
{:error :kind-mismatch, :message kind mismatch}
ok a caught error leaves the db usable
ok * cuts a card-many attribute at 1000
ok a bare spec cuts at 1000
ok :limit nil reads every value
{:error :nextomic/closed, :message the connection is released, or the with scope of this db-value has ended}
